     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1" loext:marker-style-name="T10"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935149" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">1.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T13"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">Introduction</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 4</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1" loext:marker-style-name="T10"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935150" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">2.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T13"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">How do we improve discoverability?</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 4</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_2" loext:marker-style-name="T11"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935151" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">2.1.<text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span>Make the most of the app name/title<text:span text:style-name="T16"> 6</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_2" loext:marker-style-name="T11"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935152" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">2.2.<text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span>Include plenty of keywords in the description<text:span text:style-name="T16"> 8</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_2" loext:marker-style-name="T11"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935153" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:soft-page-break/>2.3.<text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span>Use the language (or languages) that people are most likely to search with<text:span text:style-name="T16"> 8</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_2" loext:marker-style-name="T11"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935154" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">2.4.<text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span>Translate your app store page into different languages<text:span text:style-name="T16"> 8</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1" loext:marker-style-name="T10"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935155" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">3.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T13"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">How do we improve the conversion rate?</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 8</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_2" loext:marker-style-name="T11"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935156" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">3.1.<text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span>How can we improve on-metadata factors to optimise the conversion rate?<text:span text:style-name="T16"> 9</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_3" loext:marker-style-name="T12"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935157" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">3.1.1.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">App Icon</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 9</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_3" loext:marker-style-name="T12"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935158" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">3.1.2.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">Description</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 9</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_3" loext:marker-style-name="T12"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935159" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">3.1.3.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">Screenshots</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 10</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_2" loext:marker-style-name="T11"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935160" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:soft-page-break/>3.2.<text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span>How can we influence off-metadata factors to optimise the conversion rate?<text:span text:style-name="T16"> 12</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_3" loext:marker-style-name="T12"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935161" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">3.2.1.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">Number of installs</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 12</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_3" loext:marker-style-name="T12"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935162" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">3.2.2.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">Ratings</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 13</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_3" loext:marker-style-name="T12"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Toc77935163" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T3">3.2.3.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">Reviews</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> 13</text:span></text:a></text:p>
    </text:index-body>
   </text:table-of-content>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P5" text:outline-level="1" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc77935149"/><text:span text:style-name="T3">Introduction</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc77935149"/><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">You have built a great app, but can people find it, and do they want to install it?</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">When we talk about </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">App Store Optimization (ASO)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">, we focus on two things: discoverability and conversion.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum3">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P7" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T6">Discoverability</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> - making it easier for users to find your app on the app store. </text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum3">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P7" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T6">Conversion</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> - increasing the likelihood of a user installing and trying out your app once they have found it.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">In other words, we don&apos;t just want to create apps: we want people to find the apps, install them and use them. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">We will begin by looking at the area of discoverability.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc77935150"/><text:span text:style-name="T3">How do we improve discoverability?</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc77935150"/><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T3">How will users find your app on Google Play or the Apple App Store? There can be several pathways:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum4">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P8" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T6">Searching</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> in the app store, e.g. typing in keywords into the Google Play app search box, such as “Minyanka Bible”.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">Clicking on an </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">advert</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> from a marketing campaign that you have paid for, e.g. using Google Ads or Facebook Ads.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">Links from </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">other websites</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">, such as language community forums.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">Links for </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">related apps</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">, e.g. you are looking at the store page of a dictionary app and you see there is also a Bible app available for the same language, or an interesting app by the same developer.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">Recommendations from </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">friends</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">The first of these, searching using keywords in the app store is likely to be one of the major sources of new users. What can we do to increase the likelihood that someone in your target audience finds your app when searching in the store? First we need to think about the keywords they might type in the search bar, and secondly we need to make sure that as many of these keywords appear on the store page for our app.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P43" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">If your app is in </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">Google Play</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3">, the following elements on your app store page are indexed for keywords:</text:span></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum7">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">the app name/title</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">the short description (displayed on the front page for the app)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">the long description (displayed when the user taps on ‘About this app’)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T3">the app package name (not shown when viewing apps on a phone, but visible in the browser address bar when viewing on a computer)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T3">the developer name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T3"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><draw:custom-shape text:anchor-type="char" style:rel-height="20%" draw:z-index="43" draw:name="Text Box 2" draw:style-name="gr9" draw:text-style-name="P48" svg:width="1.0512in" svg:height="0.5059in" svg:x="4.978in" svg:y="1.9075in">
